+# Verification checklist: create-and-scene
+
+Merged verification plan. I-* and L-* preserve implementor and lead IDs; repeated IDs trace distinct behaviors split from aggregate rows. X-* records definition crosschecks missed by both. Source is provenance, not verification status. These are planned checks; this merge does not claim they have run.
+
+Specs: `specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md` (ESP), `specs/presentation-skill/spec.md` (PS), `specs/presentation-verification/spec.md` (PV). References are relative to this change; repository workflow/hygiene rules come from `AGENTS.md`.
+
+Only INT-001, INT-002, E2E-001 and E2E-002 from `test-plan.md` are integration/end-to-end checks. Other checks are unit/component/type tests, scripted commands, or file/artifact inspection. No check asks an agent to operate the product as a viewer. Static screenshot inspection reads script-produced artifacts. Executable helper behavior is tested when present, rather than inferred solely from skill wording.
+
+Lead rulings are recorded in `/workspace/home/.agent-runner/projects/-artifacts--runtime-candidate-worktree/runs/audited-implement-change-2026-10-18T22-38-54-57008848Z/output/acceptance-assumptions.md`. Unknown routes require Landing. Script hash parity retains the stricter check from both lists; app-owned validation data may differ without weakening reference validation or bootstrap smoke checks. Final attribution URL confirmation remains nonblocking under the recorded URL rule.
